# Host cleanup and measured optimization

Branch: `host-cleanup`, based on root `be30580` and Linux Host `b735ec86`.
Includes the pending dependency refresh and SDL-free Client work. No merge,
release or deployment is implied by candidate builds.

## Scope

1. Remove unreferenced Linux GameStream crypto helpers; preserve the HTTPS
   certificate generator and verify the generated certificate/key directly.
2. Remove the superseded macOS backend in the Linux fork and unused upstream
   packaging. Preserve attribution, supported RPM integration and shared code
   used by x264/NVENC, capture, display restoration and input.
3. Restrict the product encoder registry to the two exact supported backends;
   remove misleading unused build switches. Do not remove shared graphics/DRM
   helpers merely because KMS capture is not an offered bookmark source.
4. Compile the native macOS Host with `-O2`, without fast-math or color changes.
5. Cache stable macOS display snapshots for at most 20 ms. Invalidate
   immediately on display notifications, selection/profile changes or failed
   validation. Retain the stable double-read on refresh and the bounded refresh
   for missed notifications. Authentication and graphical ownership checks
   remain independent and uncached by this change.

## Validation

- Focused crypto/source/build-policy checks and existing Linux Host gates.
- macOS synthetic display lifecycle: unchanged fast reads, immediate notified
  invalidation, missed-event expiry, property changes, failed reads and changes
  during refresh. Compare query counts without claiming a hardware speedup.
- Hosted Rocky 9.7 RPM and SDK27/26.7 signed Host PKG builds, exact source and
  checksum collection. Reuse verified dependency caches; do not compile on
  hardware test machines.
- Installed acceptance remains required: login/logout, headless/display changes,
  audio/video soak, input/Wacom and both macOS 26.7/27. No production session
  interruption or automatic deployment in this task.

## Approved second pass — Hosts and desktop Clients

Remove the remaining unused common-C crypto and socket helpers, including the
redundant network preflight performed after the native transport connects.
Preserve thread/signal initialization and the active media/input queues. Retire
old Client renderer resources and inherited packaging/prebuilt/Qt5 paths. Move
the packed-color shader regression to the actual Qt shader source before
deleting the old shader. Remove unused controller launch arguments and the GFE
audio error translation.

On the Linux Host, remove the no-op libdisplaydevice layer and the unselected
VA-API/Vulkan encoder and Wayland/KWin/portal capture backends. Preserve DRM,
EGL/CUDA helpers, native X11 capture, and PLANK's actual display supervision.
Retire schemas4–6 from the macOS external launch protocol and the desktop
Client's finite old-release adapter; retain schema7 feature negotiation and
explicit incompatible-peer errors. Current audio, input and color policies stay
unchanged. Keep these changes in focused commits and validate all four hosted
packages, followed by installed session acceptance; do not merge or release.

## Status

The original Host cleanup and standard Mac Installer candidates passed their
hosted builds (versions1.3.02/1.3.03); exact provenance remains in HANDOFF and the
artifact manifests. The approved second pass is implemented for candidate
1.3.04, with local source, common-C lifecycle, prepared-patch and production Qt
shader checks passing. All four hosted builds passed and their candidate
packages were collected with original source provenance and checksums. Both Mac
PKGs are signed and notarized. The Linux build exposed a stale source assertion
and an unused VA-API include; both were removed or corrected before its successful
build. This completes the approved implementation and package-validation pass.
Installed session acceptance remains pending. No merge, release, deployment or
live hardware-performance claim.

See [the scope inventory](../reviews/desktop-cleanup-inventory.md) for removals,
retained callers and the explicit validation boundary. HANDOFF is current state;
older build narratives remain available through Git and artifact manifests.
